-- #1648 — NOT GRADED BY THIS GATE. Row B of the issue's table: the body uses the VALUE
-- but not the dict. Same skew, a different downstream symptom — the mis-bound parameter
-- is matched against `Box`'s pattern and no arm applies.
--
-- Measured first-hand: check 0, run `7` (the interpreter is CORRECT), build 0, and the
-- BINARY exits 1 with `runtime error [E-NONEXHAUSTIVE-MATCH]: non-exhaustive match`,
-- printing nothing.
--
-- It is kept as the third cell of the one varied dimension (does the body use the dict?)
-- and because it is the shape a reader most naturally writes when trying to reproduce
-- #1648 with an `a`-typed field present: note that ADDING the field is not what fixes the
-- crash — using it is (control.mdk). Not pinned: one issue gets one fixture, and exit 139
-- on main.mdk is the sharper observable of the same defect.
data Box a = Box a Int

interface Same a where
  bar : a -> Int

impl Same (Box a) requires Eq a where
  bar b = match b
    Box x n => n

main = println (bar (Box 1 7))
